  "Id": 2626,
  "Title": "Two New Books from AKU-ISMC Publications",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "In association with EUP",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass315FFC2562D24BD99AFFB6549CDD6C91\"><p>AKU-ISMC is delighted to announce the publication of two new books by&#160;Mohsen Kadivar; <em>Human Rights and Reformist Islam</em>, translated by Niki Akhavan and&#160;<em>Blasphemy and Apostasy in Islam&#58; Debates in Shi'a Jurisprudence</em> translated by Hamid Mavani.<br></p><p><em>Human Rights and Reformist Islam</em>&#160;translates the influential collection Haqq al-nas which argues for the compatability of human rights and Islam. &#160;<em>Blasphemy and Apostasy in Islam&#58; Debates in Shi'a Jurisprudence</em> presents a back and forth debate between two modern Shi'a jurists (one conservative, one reformist) that locates the exact points of controversy surrounding apostasy and blasphemy.<br></p><p> Both books are&#160;are published&#160;in association with Edinburgh University Press and are&#160;available to buy now with a limited offer of a 30% discount using the code NEW30. &#160;<br></p></div>",
